==Battleground==
*2 [[Duche]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*4 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s (400%) spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 30~50 seconds<sup>900f~1,500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gabriel]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**9 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**7 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**4 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Lucky Sloth]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**2 [[Dark Emperor Santa]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The large number of high damage-per-hit enemies and Angels means that one should bring [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and several cheap, disposable [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] (like [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Cat]] and other 75 cent meatshields) and/or [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] for their defense. Stall the initial wave of peons with Ramen Cat, and use suicidal damage dealers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to remove problematic peons as necessary. From there, stack [[:Category:Sniper-class Cats|Snipers]] like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] to wear down the backline alongside more close-ranged damage dealers that can deal with Red and/or Angel enemies, like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]].

